  "content": {
    "id": "p45-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "A projectile from the origin has parametric equations $x=20t$, $y=-5t^2+30t$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p45-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show the Cartesian equation is $y=\\frac32x-\\frac{1}{80}x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t=\\frac{x}{20}$ gives $y=\\frac32x-\\frac{1}{80}x^2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}t&=\\frac{x}{20}\\\\y&=-5\\left(\\frac{x}{20}\\right)^2+30\\left(\\frac{x}{20}\\right)\\\\&=\\frac32x-\\frac{1}{80}x^2\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the range and greatest height.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Range: $120$ units. Greatest height: $45$ units.",
          "worked": "For the range, set $y=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac32x-\\frac{x^2}{80}&=0\\\\x\\left(\\frac32-\\frac{x}{80}\\right)&=0\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }120\\end{aligned}$$\nThe range is $120$ units.\n\nAt the greatest height, $\\frac{dy}{dx}=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac32-\\frac{x}{40}\\\\\\frac32-\\frac{x}{40}&=0\\\\x&=60\\\\y(60)&=\\frac32(60)-\\frac{60^2}{80}\\\\&=45\\end{aligned}$$\nThe greatest height is $45$ units.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the direction of motion when $x=100$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$45^\\circ$ below the horizontal.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac32-\\frac{x}{40}\\\\\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=100}&=\\frac32-\\frac{100}{40}=-1\\\\\\tan^{-1}(1)&=45^\\circ\\end{aligned}$$\nThe horizontal velocity is $20>0$ and the slope is negative, so the direction of motion is $45^\\circ$ below the horizontal.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
